# CODEOWNERS — who is automatically requested to review what.
# Docs: https://docs.github.com/en/repositories/managing-your-repositorys-settings-and-features/customizing-your-repository/about-code-owners
#
# Location: .github/CODEOWNERS (repo root or docs/ also work).
# Rules are evaluated bottom-up; the LAST matching pattern wins.
# Replace @your-username with real users or @org/team.

# Default owner for everything not matched below.
*                       @your-username

# Repo plumbing
/.github/               @your-username

# Documentation
*.md                    @your-username
/docs/                  @your-username

# ── Split ownership example ───────────────────────────────────
# /frontend/            @your-org/frontend-team
# /backend/             @your-org/backend-team
# /infra/               @your-org/platform-team
# /migrations/          @your-org/dba-team

# ── Critical files: require a specific reviewer ───────────────
# /SECURITY.md          @your-username
# /package.json         @your-username
# /.github/workflows/   @your-username
